! TRANSMIT: what this model honours, and what it refuses out loud.
!
! WHY THIS PROGRAM EXISTS.  bsv/README.md's "decoded but not executed
! (sets indicator 15, OP, and no-ops)" list has always named "Transmit
! backward/SWAP/multi-word".  Until 2026-09-22 only BACKWARD was true:
!
!   * the decoder matched sub-ops 010 (Transmit) and 110 (Swap) in one
!     condition and recorded NEITHER -- StretchTypes' Transmit struct
!     had no `swap` field -- so a forward SWAP arrived at the execute
!     stage indistinguishable from a Transmit and was executed as one;
!   * the execute arm moves exactly one word and never looked at the
!     count, so any multi-word Transmit moved one word.
!
! Both were SILENT: no indicator, no failure, a wrong store.  Neither
! was reachable from STRAP, because this assembler could not encode
! Transmit at all until TRANSMIT_CODES landed the same day -- which is
! why a claim in the README could stay false.  Demonstrated before it
! was fixed: "SWAPI,1,SRC,DST" left SRC alone and copied it into DST
! (0x9249249249249249) with OP clear.
!
! WHAT THE MANUAL SAYS THE COUNT IS.  Reference Manual pp.30-31: the
! count is index J's bits 28-45, 0 meaning 2^18; or, with the
! immediate modifier (bit 56), instruction bits 51-54, where **0 MEANS
! SIXTEEN**.  So the only count this arm can honour is immediate-and-
! -one; TI,0 is a sixteen-word transmit and must be refused, which is
! the case a "j == 0 means no words" reading would get wrong.
!
! A DIRECT COUNT IS REFUSED WHOLESALE, and that is deliberately
! conservative: the count register is never read here, so the arm
! cannot know whether a direct count is one.  It therefore refuses a
! direct count of one that it would have executed correctly, rather
! than executing a direct count of n as one word.  Stated in the
! execute arm.
!
! THE CASE THAT KEEPS THIS HONEST is the first one.  If the fix were
! "OP on everything", block 1 would fail: TI with an immediate count
! of one must STILL STORE, and that is the shape jb_ax5b p.45 actually
! uses (ax5b_16087_walk.strap).
!
! EACH BLOCK ISOLATES ONE RULE, and that is not decorative: the
! program hangs at the FIRST failing block, so an injection breaking
! several is only ever observed at the earliest.  The four injections
! recorded in run_tests.sh therefore target one block each.
!
! WEAKER STANDARD: hand-written from Reference Manual pp.30-31 and the
! pocket card's TRANSMIT box.  No listing prints a SWAP or a
! multi-word Transmit anywhere this project has read.

        SLC, (8)4100.0
!
! ---- 1. TI, immediate count 1: HONOURED, the word moves -----------
START   TI,    1, SRC, DST1
        BOP,   $                     ! hang if OP came on: this one is legal
!
! ---- 2. SWAPI: refused.  The case that was silently wrong ---------
        SWAPI, 1, SRC, DST2
        BZOP,  $                     ! hang if OP did NOT come on
        BOPZ,  $+.32                 ! clear OP for the next case
!
! ---- 3. TI, immediate count 2: refused, multi-word ----------------
        TI,    2, SRC, DST3
        BZOP,  $
        BOPZ,  $+.32
!
! ---- 4. TI, immediate count 0 = SIXTEEN (pp.30-31): refused -------
! The case a "0 means none" reading gets wrong.
        TI,    0, SRC, DST4
        BZOP,  $
        BOPZ,  $+.32
!
! ---- 5. T, DIRECT count: refused, the count register is unread ----
        T,     1, SRC, DST5
        BZOP,  $
        BOPZ,  $+.32
!
! ---- 6. TBI, backward: refused.  This check already existed, and is
!         here so that removing it fails a test ---------------------
! IT MUST BE TBI, NOT TB, and that was found by the injection rather
! than by thinking.  TB is backward with a DIRECT count, so the count
! rule refuses it too -- removing the backward check changed nothing
! and the whole block still passed.  TBI is backward with an
! immediate count of one, so oneWordForward is TRUE and the backward
! check is the ONLY thing that can refuse it.
        TBI,   1, SRC, DST6
        BZOP,  $
        BOPZ,  $+.32
        B, PASS
PASS    BEW, $
!
! ---- data ---------------------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)4200.0
SRC     DD(BU,64,8), (8)1111111111111111111111
        SLC, (8)4201.0
DST1    DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! must RECEIVE src
        SLC, (8)4202.0
DST2    DD(BU,64,8), 0               ! must stay zero
        SLC, (8)4203.0
DST3    DD(BU,64,8), 0
        SLC, (8)4204.0
DST4    DD(BU,64,8), 0
        SLC, (8)4205.0
DST5    DD(BU,64,8), 0
        SLC, (8)4206.0
DST6    DD(BU,64,8), 0
        END, START
